{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#775","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#775","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#775\",\"parent_revision\":\"834b7d033d64a2aa4793c0a34784eca91c7df903c9b5a75bab607d1c85ad22be\",\"root_revision\":\"834b7d033d64a2aa4793c0a34784eca91c7df903c9b5a75bab607d1c85ad22be\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Current state**: The `task_status_hook.py` writes an ephemeral context file at `.claude/context/active-task-{session_id}.json` containing `task_file_path`, `task_id`, and optionally `parent_issue_number`. This file is deleted by the SubagentStop hook when the sub-agent finishes. The `LastActivity` timestamp is written to the task file's YAML frontmatter on each Write/Edit/Bash call. Once a session ends, there is no persistent record of which agent worked on which task, what skills were loaded, how many tool calls were made, or what the agent's final output summary was. Cross-session context recovery relies entirely on reading the task file's status fields and any code changes committed.\\n\\n**Target state**: The SubagentStop hook, before deleting the active-task context file, appends a structured session summary record to a persistent file at `.claude/context/session-history.jsonl`. Each record contains: `session_id`, `task_id`, `task_file_path`, `agent_type`, `skills_loaded` (list), `started` (ISO timestamp from task), `completed` (ISO timestamp), `last_activity` (ISO timestamp), `parent_issue_number` (if known), and `outcome` (COMPLETE or the final status). This file accumulates across sessions and is never deleted by hooks.\\n\\n**Measurable signal**: File `.claude/context/session-history.jsonl` exists after at least one SubagentStop event. Each line is valid JSON containing at minimum `session_id`, `task_id`, `agent_type`, `completed`, and `outcome` fields. Running `wc -l .claude/context/session-history.jsonl` returns a count equal to the number of completed sub-agent sessions.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Persistent structured session metadata for cross-session context recovery\\nDate: 2026-04-23\\nGoal: Append a structured session summary to a persistent history file at SubagentStop before deleting the ephemeral context file, enabling cross-session context recovery.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. task_status_hook.py SubagentStop handler | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py\\n2. active-task context file structure | AVAILABLE | written at .claude/context/active-task-{session_id}.json with task_file_path, task_id, parent_issue_number\\n3. session-history.jsonl write location | AVAILABLE | .claude/context/session-history.jsonl (new file per design)\\n4. Fields available at SubagentStop | AVAILABLE | session_id, task_id, task_file_path, agent_type from context file; completed timestamp derivable; outcome from task YAML\\n5. skills_loaded and tool_call_count fields | DERIVABLE | not currently in context file; may require hook enhancement to track these during session\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 core fields available; skills_loaded is optional and can be omitted if not tracked.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler appends a JSONL record to `.claude/context/session-history.jsonl` BEFORE deleting the active-task context file\\n- [ ] Each record contains at minimum: `session_id`, `task_id`, `task_file_path`, `agent_type`, `started`, `completed`, `last_activity`, `parent_issue_number`, `outcome`\\n- [ ] The file is NOT deleted by any hook; it accumulates across sessions\\n- [ ] `wc -l .claude/context/session-history.jsonl` equals the number of SubagentStop events that fired in prior sessions\\n- [ ] Each line is valid JSON (verify: `python3 -c \\\"import json, sys; [json.loads(l) for l in sys.stdin]\\\" < .claude/context/session-history.jsonl` exits 0)\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/ -k session_history -x` passes (test: SubagentStop simulation writes correct record; file is appended not overwritten on second run)\\n- [ ] `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 zero errors\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 SubagentStop handler (primary change)\\n- `.claude/context/session-history.jsonl` (new persistent file \u2014 gitignored or committed as part of session state)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/` \u2014 test for session-history append behavior\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a **developer starting a new session after a previous subagent completed work**, I want **a persistent `session-history.jsonl` file that survived hook cleanup** so that **I can reconstruct what the previous agent did without reading the full JSONL transcript**.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **persistent structured session metadata for cross-session context recovery** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/sidecar.md -- pattern: Context Window Recovery via persistent session history\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-17\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e0a9742bdf87ca617b590ea8bce40f016a6e52504991f5774bebb656c5435f69\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTEN1g\"}"}